This solution uses a breadth-first search (BFS) approach to simulate the rotting process. It initializes a queue with all the rotten oranges and counts the number of fresh oranges. Then, it iteratively rots all adjacent fresh oranges from the current set of rotten oranges, updating the grid and reducing the fresh count. The process continues until no more oranges can be rotted, and the function returns the number of minutes passed minus one (since the last iteration might not have any new rotting). If there are still fresh oranges left after processing, it returns -1 indicating that they cannot be rotted.
